    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Welcome to this spacious detached bungalow set on a private site in the peaceful countryside of Glanmire, offering an excellent balance of rural tranquillity and convenient access to nearby amenities.\r\nExtending to approximately 168 sq.m., this generously proportioned home offers flexible family accommodation with excellent potential for updating and modernisation throughout.\r\n\r\nThe property is entered via a welcoming front porch leading into a bright and spacious interior. To the front of the home is a separate living room, creating a cosy and private reception space, while a large family room positioned centrally within the property provides an additional living area ideal for everyday family life and entertaining. The kitchen and adjoining dining area form the heart of the home, complemented by a separate utility/laundry room for added practicality.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises six bedrooms in total, including a spacious primary bedroom positioned to the rear of the property. One of the bedrooms is currently being used for storage, offering flexibility for a home office, playroom, or additional guest accommodation. A long central hallway enhances the sense of space and connects the living and sleeping accommodation throughout the home. Multiple bathroom facilities further add to the practicality of the layout.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property benefits from private parking and surrounding outdoor space with excellent potential to further enhance the gardens and exterior areas to suit individual tastes.\r\n\r\nHeating is currently provided via a solid fuel back boiler system, while the option for oil-fired central heating is also available, although this would require reconnection.\r\n\r\nWhile the property would benefit from refurbishment and modernisation, it presents a fantastic opportunity for buyers seeking to create a substantial family home in a scenic countryside setting.\r\n\r\nLocated just a short drive from Glanmire village and within easy reach of Cork City, the property enjoys the best of both worlds — peaceful rural living while remaining convenient to schools, shops, cafés, sporting facilities, and major road networks.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The above details are for guidance only and are not part of any contract. They are prepared with care, but we are not responsible for inaccuracies. All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition, necessary permission for use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith. They are believed to be correct, but any intending purchaser or tenant should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to their correctness. If there is any inconsistency between these particulars and the contract of sale, the latter shall prevail. The details are issued on the understanding that all negotiations on any property are done through this office."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
